  "requirement": "Use macOS MCP before computer-use models; preserve the entire task across independent approvals, login handoff, Resume and Stop without replay.",
  "implemented": [
    "MCP approval continuation can opt into the existing immutable ordered-action plan and ledger. Legacy one-action executors retain their prior path.",
    "The host records each confirmed effect before asking the retained adapter for the next step, a manual-control handoff, or verified completion. It checks the exact stored plan, confirmed prefix, next effect ID/call digest and remaining approved steps. Uncertain effects are not repeated.",
    "Capability wrappers retain the same desktop route for ordered plans. Resume continues from recorded effects, with cancellation and host control gates around continuation.",
    "ExecutionContext retains the original signed request body separately from model input, across handback and visual replanning. This binds approval plans to the correct durable request identity and preserves client evidence opt-ins.",
    "Confirmed evidence is published before an asynchronous continuation can pause or be stopped; late work cannot authorize another action."
  ],
